                "notes": "identifier CHEBI:31795 -> cas:14168-73-1; ontology_id CHEBI:31795 -> CHEBI:32599; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is magnesium sulfate monohydrate (TogoMedium M2312 lists the ingredient as GMO_001587 'Magnesium sulfate monohydrate') but was grounded to CHEBI:31795, the heptahydrate. Search for a monohydrate term, 2026-10-15: local ChEBI release 255 (labels and synonyms naming magnesium sulfate with monohydrate, (1/1), hydrate or kieserite; formulas H2MgO5S and Mg.O4S.H2O; xrefs to CAS 14168-73-1) found only the heptahydrate CHEBI:31795; OLS4 ChEBI release 256 returned no hits for 'magnesium sulfate monohydrate' or 'kieserite', and 'magnesium sulfate' returned only CHEBI:32599 and CHEBI:31795. So the record takes its own CAS, cas:14168-73-1 (PubChem CID 16211255 'Magnesium sulfate monohydrate'), with skos:broadMatch to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:32599 and the Rule B1 registry row kgmicrobe.compound:mgso4h2o (MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 step 2)."
